      "proof_trace": "The Discord guild membership check (fetchMemberStatus call) is explicitly commented out at L105-119 of the auth callback, allowing any Discord OAuth user with a valid member.members DB record to establish a Supabase session without server membership verification. The compensating control in dashboard/layout.tsx (L129-133) is fail-open: the guard condition `discordCheck.success && !discordCheck.isInServer` evaluates to false when the STEM Bot API returns a non-2xx HTTP response (success: false), silently granting dashboard access to expelled users during any API degradation. The checkDiscordMembership function (actions.ts:L1256-1258) returns {success: false} for non-ok responses rather than throwing, bypassing the catch block's redirect.",
      "attack_scenario": "A user who has been removed from the Discord server but retains a member.members DB record completes the Discord OAuth PKCE flow, exchanges the authorization code at /auth/callback to obtain a valid Supabase session, then accesses /dashboard during any period when the STEM Bot API returns a non-2xx HTTP status — causing checkDiscordMembership to return {success: false, isInServer: false}, bypassing the layout-level guild check and granting full dashboard access.",
      "checklist_id": "PROP-attendanceze-inv-006"
    },
    "text": "Discord server membership check must be enforced (currently commented out per INV-004).",
    "assertion": "forall user: authCallback(user) => discord_guild_member_check(user.discord_uid) == true",
    "covers": "SG-005",
    "severity": "HIGH",
    "type": "invariant"
  }
}

